  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Fairleigh Dickinson University (FDU) Vancouver Campus offers you a unique opportunity to earn an American college degree while studying in Canada. As a comprehensive, not-for-profit university, the campus delivers industry-aligned undergraduate and graduate education in fields including business, information technology, hospitality and tourism, and the humanities. Since its establishment in 2007, the campus has welcomed students from more than 60 countries, fostering a culturally diverse learning environment.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>At FDU Vancouver, you will be part of a vibrant, globally minded community. The university is committed to providing comprehensive student support services, including wellness resources and assistance for those needing to develop English-language skills before starting degree studies. You will find a dedicated faculty and staff from all corners of the globe, ensuring you feel supported throughout your academic journey.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>The university provides resources to help you find suitable housing in the city. If you are looking for accommodation, please check the official FDU Vancouver website for the latest guidance on housing options to help you settle into life in Vancouver. If you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, feel free to <a href=\"https://onelink.to/jb48ev\">download our app</a> and check out the <a href=\"https://edvoy.com/student/stays\">Stays</a> feature!&nbsp;</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<ol><li><strong>Library</strong> You will have access to library resources and academic support necessary to facilitate your research and learning needs.</li><li><strong>Sports</strong> The university emphasizes overall student well-being and provides access to resources and activities that support a healthy, balanced lifestyle.</li><li><strong>Laboratories</strong> You will have access to modern learning environments designed to support your practical training and academic projects.</li><li><strong>Cafeteria</strong> There are various dining options available in the surrounding downtown Vancouver area, allowing you to enjoy a wide range of fresh food and beverages near your campus.</li></ol>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Campuses",
      "value": "<p><strong>Vancouver</strong></p><p>The Vancouver Campus is located in downtown Vancouver, British Columbia. It provides an accessible, urban learning environment well-connected to the city's business community and cultural attractions. In the fall of 2026, the campus is scheduled to move to a new, state-of-the-art facility at Oakridge Park, which will further enhance opportunities for collaboration, innovation, and connection with local industry partners.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
